        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): add estimate-before-decode guard to base64 paths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLarge base64-encoded images can cause transient memory pressure during decoding. This PR adds a size estimation check before decoding base64 image data in CLI staging and provider image-parsing paths, and propagates the existing configured media size limit through these new guards.\n\n**Security impact**: Defense-in-depth against transient memory exhaustion from oversized base64 payloads.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Added `estimateBase64DecodedSize` helper that estimates decoded byte length from base64 input\n- Propagated existing `maxBytes` limit through:\n  - CLI image writing (`writeCliImages`)\n  - Provider image parsing (`generatedImageAssetFromBase64`)\n- Added boundary tests for:\n  - Configured limit acceptance (7MB payload under 8MB limit)\n  - Over-limit rejection before decoding\n  - Default limit enforcement (6 MiB)\n- **No new configuration**: Uses existing `generatedMediaMaxBytes` setting\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Environment**: macOS Vitest (Node 22.22.2)\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n```bash\n# Run configured limit test\nnpx vitest run src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts\n```\n\n**Observed result after fix**:\n```text\n✓ agents-core src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts (30 tests) 203ms\n✓ agents-support src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts (30 tests) 184ms\n\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  60 passed (60)\n\nKey test coverage:\n✓ rejects base64 image that exceeds size limit\n✓ accepts images above MAX_IMAGE_BYTES when a higher configured maxBytes is provided\n  - 7MB payload accepted under 8MB configured limit (line 322-346)\n  - 10MB payload rejected under 8MB limit\n  - 7MB payload rejected under default 6MiB limit (no maxBytes)\n```\n\n**Configuration limit propagation verified**:\n- Test file: `src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts:322-346`\n- Scenario: 7MB payload (above default 6MiB) accepted when 8MB limit configured\n- Code path: `writeCliImages` receives `maxBytes: 8 * 1024 * 1024`, checks pass\n\n**What was not tested**: Live provider OOM reproduction (neither necessary nor safely desirable)\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n- Coverage: 60 tests across 2 test suites\n- Target files: `src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts`, `src/image-generation/image-assets.test.ts`\n- Scenarios locked in:\n  - Estimated size < maxBytes: accept\n  - Estimated size > maxBytes: reject before decode\n  - Configured limit > default: use configured\n  - No configured limit: use default 6 MiB\n",
        "branch": "fix/base64-decode-before-bounds-unified",
